{"schema":3,"schemaVersion":3,"buildId":"v212-d99509bea02c69","words":{"shale":{"word":"shale","nativeZh":["n. 页岩"],"senses":[{"id":"wn30:shale%1:27:00::","pos":"n","en":"a sedimentary rock formed by the deposition of successive layers of clay","zh":"由连续层粘土沉积形成的沉积岩","labelZh":"泥板岩；页岩","domainZh":"物质","domainEn":"Substances","translation":"machine","source":"WordNet 3.0","examples":[],"sourceRefs":[{"source":"WordNet","version":"3.0","synsetId":"15038520-n","senseKey":"shale%1:27:00::"}],"pairId":"54ead458afd64c26486b8562","reviewStatus":"machine_screened","qualityIssues":[]}],"phrases":[],"examples":[],"relations":[],"wordId":"en:shale","nativeSourceSummary":{"zh":["n. 页岩"],"pairs":[{"sourceText":"n. 页岩","sourceTextHash":"0f374ab3ce8b9667a73b0938d41ff7876e4d04188d6a4683d06a461b4cfd8b79","id":"native:shale:0f374ab3ce8b9667a7","zh":"n. 页岩","en":"noun: a sedimentary rock formed by the deposition of successive layers of clay","translation":"dictionary","cacheKey":"2d9b1cb1949a1e3e75187d91347421b8b5d401ab67232202eb380068d2ddd7e9","contextHash":"81bf2f52a5b6f757b96f4d47bf2113465555d0edcf6da91b398013d392fba28a","counterpartMethod":"exact_cow_label_mapping","sourceRefs":[{"source":"ECDICT","version":"local-frozen-20261026","sourceTextHash":"0f374ab3ce8b9667a73b0938d41ff7876e4d04188d6a4683d06a461b4cfd8b79"},{"source":"Chinese Open Wordnet + Princeton WordNet","version":"PWN3.0-compatible","synsetId":"15038520-n","chineseLabel":"页岩"}],"segmentAlignment":[{"zh":"页岩","en":"a sedimentary rock formed by the deposition of successive layers of clay","originalSourceEn":"a sedimentary rock formed by the deposition of successive layers of clay","sourceSynsetIds":["15038520-n"]}],"pairId":"2fa1f87e566e0d6326f3972c","reviewStatus":"source_bilingual","qualityIssues":[]}],"archivedSourceErrors":[],"source":"ECDICT","alignmentStatus":"independent_bilingual_source_blocks","note":"Exact source blocks are paired independently with word-bound provenance; no positional WordNet mapping is asserted."}},"shall":{"word":"shall","nativeZh":["aux. 将"],"senses":[{"id":"ecdict:shall:f4a1d143e46aa1da28","pos":"v","en":"i. & auxiliary. To owe; to be under obligation for.","zh":"(一) 辅助。欠债;需承担债务。","translation":"machine","domainZh":"词典补充","domainEn":"Additional dictionary sense","source":"ECDICT","sourceRefs":[{"source":"ECDICT","version":"local-frozen-20261026","sourceTextHash":"5b7873c2c3cf8e55647feabe2f802cbce15172f3f88478f247f443caeaee0a8d"}],"pairId":"6942a3e63720bc7170e0ecbf","reviewStatus":"machine_screened","qualityIssues":[]},{"id":"ecdict:shall:899b4821a89c046c34","pos":"v","en":"i. & auxiliary. To be obliged; must.","zh":"一. 辅助,必须承担义务。","translation":"machine","domainZh":"词典补充","domainEn":"Additional dictionary sense","source":"ECDICT","sourceRefs":[{"source":"ECDICT","version":"local-frozen-20261026","sourceTextHash":"aa8fcff8c572b565198cbd0d47eb01f02343acef2260f3b995d5b2b67e37e7b7"}],"pairId":"89e1a05c197f0026273e1c27","reviewStatus":"machine_screened","qualityIssues":[]},{"id":"ecdict:shall:143ebb3e69fa9d7558","pos":"v","en":"i. & auxiliary. As an auxiliary, shall indicates a duty or necessity whose obligation is derived from the person speaking; as, you shall go; he shall go; that is, I order or promise your going. It thus ordinarily expresses, in the second and third persons, a command, a threat, or a promise. If the auxillary be emphasized, the command is made more imperative, the promise or that more positive and sure. It is also employed in the language of prophecy; as, \"the day shall come when . . . , \" since a promise or threat and an authoritative prophecy nearly coincide in significance. In shall with the first person, the necessity of the action is sometimes implied as residing elsewhere than in the speaker; as, I shall suffer; we shall see; and there is always a less distinct and positive assertion of his volition than is indicated by will. \"I shall go\" implies nearly a simple futurity; more exactly, a foretelling or an expectation of my going, in which, naturally enough, a certain degree of plan or intention may be included; emphasize the shall, and the event is described as certain to occur, and the expression approximates in meaning to our emphatic \"I will go.\" In a question, the relation of speaker and source of obligation is of course transferred to the person addressed; as, \"Shall you go?\" (answer, \"I shall go\"); \"Shall he go?\" i. e., \"Do you require or promise his going?\" (answer, \"He shall go\".) The same relation is transferred to either second or third person in such phrases as \"You say, or think, you shall go;\" \"He says, or thinks, he shall go.\" After a conditional conjunction (as if, whether) shall is used in all persons to express futurity simply; as, if I, you, or he shall say they are right. Should is everywhere used in the same connection and the same senses as shall, as its imperfect. It also expresses duty or moral obligation; as, he should do it whether he will or not. In the early English, and hence in our English Bible, shall is the auxiliary mainly used, in all the persons, to express simple futurity. (Cf. Will, v. t.) Shall may be used elliptically; thus, with an adverb or other word expressive of motion go may be omitted.","zh":"不及物动词及助动词的旧词典用法说明。作为助动词，shall可以表示出自说话者意志的义务或必要性。例如you shall go、he shall go可以表示我命令你或他去，或我保证你或他会去。因此它在第二、第三人称中常表达命令、威胁或承诺。重读shall时，命令更强，承诺或威胁也更为肯定。它也用于预言，例如the day shall come when…表示总有一天……；承诺、威胁与权威性预言的意义彼此接近。与第一人称连用时，行动的必要性有时来自说话者之外，例如I shall suffer、we shall see；相比will，它通常较少明确表达说话者的意志。I shall go通常接近单纯的将来，确切地说是预告或预期自己将去，其中也可能包含计划或意图；重读shall，则表示事情确定会发生，接近强调的I will go。在问句中，决定或承担义务的主体转为受问者，例如Shall you go?可答I shall go；Shall he go?可理解为你要求或保证他去吗，可答He shall go。相同关系也见于You say or think you shall go和He says or thinks he shall go等句式。在if、whether等条件或疑问连接词之后，shall可用于各个人称单纯表示将来，例如if I, you, or he shall say they are right。should作为shall的过去式，可用于相同结构和意义，也表示职责或道德义务，例如he should do it whether he will or not，即无论他愿不愿意都应该做。在早期英语及旧式英语《圣经》中，shall是各个人称表达单纯将来时常用的助动词，另可参见will词条。shall也可省略使用，例如句中已有表示移动的副词或其他词语时，可省去go。","translation":"edited","domainZh":"词典补充","domainEn":"Additional dictionary sense","source":"ECDICT","sourceRefs":[{"source":"ECDICT","version":"local-frozen-20261026","sourceTextHash":"0a7e44f83d67a3a694008f48fa0e3df7c912242c2e13d539df27edb2b431f37d"}],"pairId":"ed11de6884a4e9be1814ebc4","reviewStatus":"editorial","qualityIssues":[]}],"phrases":[],"examples":[],"relations":[],"wordId":"en:shall","nativeSourceSummary":{"zh":["aux. 将"],"pairs":[{"sourceText":"aux. 将","sourceTextHash":"56682e2bd6d29cb80a79ecf23092c829465277876ce9618fe06cfee57eee2720","id":"native:shall:56682e2bd6d29cb80a","zh":"aux. 将","en":"I'm sorry, aux.","translation":"machine-en","cacheKey":"0a6e82042bc1eb34b5a4b4bda5b9535c7d3f72698149bdf9d28bf2da4dd2acea","contextHash":"78f37dc73e7502fbb9609cc6ea3682dabebb13a4a3c5f916a104a38558237636","counterpartMethod":"segmented_local_mt","sourceRefs":[{"source":"ECDICT","version":"local-frozen-20261026","sourceTextHash":"56682e2bd6d29cb80a79ecf23092c829465277876ce9618fe06cfee57eee2720"}],"sourceSegments":[{"text":"aux. 将","start":0,"end":6,"en":"I'm sorry, aux."}],"pairId":"11fa92e5190b63f8dab128ef","reviewStatus":"machine_screened","qualityIssues":[]}],"archivedSourceErrors":[],"source":"ECDICT","alignmentStatus":"independent_bilingual_source_blocks","note":"Exact source blocks are paired independently with word-bound provenance; no positional WordNet mapping is asserted."}},"shallot":{"word":"shallot","nativeZh":["n. 葱"],"senses":[{"id":"wn30:shallot%1:20:02::","pos":"n","en":"aggregate bulb of the multiplier onion","zh":"倍数洋葱的集合灯泡","labelZh":"","domainZh":"植物","domainEn":"Plants","translation":"machine","source":"WordNet 3.0","examples":[],"sourceRefs":[{"source":"WordNet","version":"3.0","synsetId":"12433429-n","senseKey":"shallot%1:20:02::"}],"pairId":"d735dddfb5100d444cdfa374","reviewStatus":"machine_screened","qualityIssues":[]},{"id":"wn30:shallot%1:20:00::","pos":"n","en":"type of onion plant producin